  "summary": [
    "Early-2026 data show an unusually high death pace in the Mediterranean, with 606 deaths by late February.",
    "Several factors push the likelihood of reaching 900 deaths by end-April: ongoing elevated risk from weather, higher departure pressure from North Africa, and persistent SAR/policy dynamics that can increase fatalities.",
    "Potential mitigating factors exist (improved SAR or safer routes), but current signals emphasize risk amplification; data revisions could also raise tallies further.",
    "Calibrated posterior reflects strong confidence in reaching the 900-death threshold within the March–April window under the observed pace."
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "narrative": "Using the high early-2026 pace as a strong anchor, multiple risk drivers point toward reaching or exceeding 900 Mediterranean deaths by end-April. While rescue improvements could curb deaths, the current momentum and weather-related risks substantially elevate the odds, yielding a posterior near 0.98 with a tight calibration range.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.75,
      "basis": "reference class anchored to early-2026 pace data (Jan–Feb 2026) and historical patterns suggesting a high likelihood of 900 deaths by end-April if the ongoing pace persists."
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "Sustained high early-2026 Mediterranean death toll pace",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "606 deaths by late February indicate momentum that makes 900 deaths by end-April plausible if the pace continues."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Storms and severe weather increasing crossing risks in Jan–Mar 2026",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Dangerous weather heightens crossing risk and fatalities, contributing to the probability of surpassing 900."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Rising departures from North Africa driving more crossings",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Increased departures (Tunisia/Libya) raise exposure on dangerous crossings, supporting higher tolls."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Policy and SAR capacity constraints / restrictive policies",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Operational constraints can elevate fatalities per crossing, pushing totals higher than unconstrained pace."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Improvements in SAR and safe-route options could reduce deaths",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "If safer routes or enhanced SAR capacity materialize, the toll could be lower than the trend suggests; this serves as a counterbalance."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "Anchored to a high early-2026 pace, the combination of multiple up-drivers yields a strong push toward 900 deaths by end-April. Correlations among pace, weather, and departures amplify effects, while a moderate down-factor (SAR improvements) provides some calibration. Given the strength and coherence of the positive signals, a posterior near 0.98 is warranted, with a narrow uncertainty range reflecting potential reporting lags and revisions."
  }
}

